um 'Anastasia'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":123875,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Chrysanthemum</em> 'Anastasia' (21c)","isAgm":false,"isSynonym":true,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":80275,"botanicalName":"<em>Dendranthema</em> 'Cottage Pink'","entityDescription":"A woody-based perennial, producing stems to 90cm high and a spread of 50cm, with deeply divided, aromatic green leaves. In late summer and autumn, the plants produce sprays of fully-double, pale pink flowers with quilled petals. They are pale purplish-pink on the undersides creating a two-tone effect","image":"sepa01707.jpg","commonName":"chrysanthemum 'Emperor of China'","nurseriesCount":10,"synonymParentPlantId":123994,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Chrysanthemum</em> 'Emperor of China' (21)","isAgm":false,"isSynonym":true,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":62963,"botanicalName":"<em>Dendranthema</em> 'Daniel Cooper'","entityDescription":"A woody-based tender perennial, producing stems to 90cm high and a spread of 50cm, with deeply divided, aromatic leaves, dark-green above and greyish-green on the reverse. In late summer and autumn, the plants produce sprays of single, mid-pink flowers with a yellow eye","image":"","commonName":"chrysanthemum 'Daniel Cooper'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":123344,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Chrysanthemum</em> 'Daniel Cooper' (21d)","isAgm":true,"isSynonym":true,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":43926,"botanicalName":"<em>Dendranthema</em> 'Duchess of Edinburgh'","entityDescription":"An erect, woody-based, deciduous perennial, producing stems to 90cm (3ft) high and a spread of 50cm (20in), with deeply divided, aromatic leaves, dark-green above and greyish-green on the reverse. In late summer and autumn, the plants produce sprays of semi-double, bright red flowers with a yellow eye. The flowers are long lasting in water and are ideal to grow for cutting. The plants are winter hardy throughout most 